h_curriculum_factory/results/v3/N32_WORKBOOK_TERMINALS.receipt.v1.json\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"PASSED\\\"}}\\nDo not read historical result Markdown or old evidence unless the node prompt names a specific file needed to diagnose a failure.\\nComplete the node's own TEST/LOOP before returning. The controller independently verifies the focused test command.\\n\\n--- BEGIN NODE PROMPT (verbatim) ---\\n# GOAL\\n\\nImplement `N40_CLI_CUTOVER` after N32. Make `python3 -m runtime.run_curriculum`\\nthe sole production entry to the compiled Plan 26 LangGraph factory.\\n\\nThe CLI may parse/validate syntax, canonicalize paths, acquire the output lock,\\nprepare the episode invocation, build the graph once, invoke it, cross-check its\\nstructured output against terminal/evidence ledgers, print one JSON object, and\\nmap exit codes. It may not run product steps, inspect results to invent routing,\\ninfer acceptance, or fall back to Plan 25/custom FSM/simulation/session bridge.\\n\\nImplement exact preflight, one, all, and resume commands/collision rules from\\nspec section 16. Historical modules may remain only when unreachable from the\\nproduction import/call graph.\\n\\n# TEST\\n\\n1. Static and runtime call-graph proof shows one production graph builder/path.\\n2. CLI help exposes no legacy simulation/session-bridge/custom-controller path.\\n3. Mode mutual exclusions, arguments, canonical paths, collision/resume rules,\\n   stdout JSON, stderr diagnostics, and exit codes match the spec.\\n4. Preflight is read-only and cannot emit product success.\\n5. CLI code contains no product nodes, guards, joins, acceptance, or frontier selection.\\n6. Missing authorization/capability fails before transmission and never simulates.\\n7. Existing Plan 25 roots are readable history but refused for Plan 26 resume.\\n8. Production import audit rejects LangChain wrappers/provider SDKs/direct model HTTP.\\n\\nWrite `results/N40_CLI_CUTOVER.result.v1.md` with CLI/call-graph proof,\\nmigration disposition, commands, and hashes.\\n\\n# LOOP\\n\\nPatch one parser, invocation helper, graph builder wiring, output verifier,\\nexit mapping, reachability test, or documentation owner. Do not delete user\\nhistory to pass scans. Stop if a second production path remains reachable.\\n\\n\\n\\n--- BEGIN APPROVED IMMUTABLE PATCH OVERLAY ---\\nPatch ID: P-N40-001\\nReason: N40's own prior result report disclosed that tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py tests the retired Plan 25 parser_for/--lab-id CLI surface and fails to import against the new build_parser()-based CLI, but the file was outside N40's write set at the time. The write set now includes it (ownership correction); N40 must retire/rewrite the stale assertions rather than leaving a downstream node to route around a collection-blocking import error it did not cause.\\nExpected effect: tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py imports cleanly and asserts the Plan 26 migration contract (parser_for absent, legacy flags rejected, no Plan 25 symbols reachable) instead of the retired Plan 25 dispatch behavior, unblocking pytest -q tests/runtime collection for all downstream full-suite runs\\nInstructions:\\nOwnership correction. This node's own prior result report already disclosed,\\ncorrectly and explicitly, that `tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py` tests\\nthe retired Plan 25 CLI surface (`parser_for(runtime)`, `--lab-id` dispatch to\\na mocked `CurriculumFactoryGraph`/`CodexWorker`) and fails to import against\\nthe new CLI, but was out of this node's write set at the time so it could not\\nbe fixed. That file is now in this node's write set. Retire/rewrite it here,\\nas the node whose CLI cutover the file's own assertions have gone stale\\nagainst.\\n\\n`tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py` currently has two independent parts:\\n\\n1. `RunCurriculumParserTests` and its shared top-of-file import\\n   `from runtime.run_curriculum import main, parser_for` \\u2014 this is what is\\n   broken. `parser_for` no longer exists; `run_curriculum.py` now exposes only\\n   `build_parser()` (no arguments, a different and much smaller flag surface:\\n   `--engine-root`, `--curriculum`, `--output-root`, one of\\n   `--preflight`/`--unit`/`--all`/`--resume`, `--authorization`). Replace this\\n   class with new tests asserting the Plan 26 migration contract instead of\\n   testing removed behavior:\\n   - `parser_for` remains absent: importing it from `runtime.run_curriculum`\\n     fails (e.g. `assertRaises(ImportError)` around the import, or\\n     `assertFalse(hasattr(run_curriculum_module, \\\"parser_for\\\"))`).\\n   - Legacy CLI surfaces remain rejected: flags the old parser accepted\\n     (`--lab-id`, and the old per-lab/per-run policy flags such as\\n     `--max-model-calls-per-lab`, `--max-concurrency`,\\n     `--max-meta-revision-cycles`, `--retry-malformed-output`) are not\\n     recognized by the current `build_parser()` and raise `SystemExit(2)`\\n     when passed.\\n   - `runtime/run_curriculum.py` uses only the Plan 26 LangGraph path: no\\n     Plan 25 symbol (`CurriculumFactoryGraph`, `CodexWorker`, `GeminiReviewer`,\\n     `runtime.controller.CurriculumRuntime`, `runtime.session_bridge`, or\\n     `parser_for`) is imported or referenced by the module. Prefer a static\\n     check (e.g. AST or source inspection of `runtime/run_curriculum.py`),\\n     consistent with the import-audit style already used in\\n     `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py`, over importing those symbols into the\\n     test itself.\\n   Do not restore `parser_for`, `CurriculumFactoryGraph`, `CodexWorker`, or any\\n   Plan 25 dispatch path in `runtime/run_curriculum.py` to make old assertions\\n   pass. The old behavior is retired; the test must assert that it stays\\n   retired, not resurrect it.\\n\\n2. `RunCurriculumElapsedTimeTests` \\u2014 this class does not import or use\\n   `parser_for`/`main` at all; it drives `runtime.controller.CurriculumRuntime\\n   .simulate(...)` directly, a historical module this node's own migration\\n   disposition deliberately left in place and unreachable from the production\\n   CLI (see this node's existing result report, \\\"Migration disposition\\\"\\n   section). It is collateral damage from sharing a file with the broken\\n   import, not itself broken. Leave this class's body untouched. The only\\n   change needed for it is fixing the shared import line at the top of the\\n   file so it no longer imports the removed `parser_for` name.\\n\\nDo not touch any file outside this node's declared write set. Do not weaken\\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py` or `tests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py`\\nto route around anything. Run the updated verification command\\n(`{python} -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py\\ntests/runtime/test_plan26_workbook.py tests/runtime/test_run_curriculum.py`)\\nand confirm it is green before finishing. Update this node's own result\\nreport to record this correction: what was wrong, why it is this node's\\nresponsibility, and what changed.\\n--- END APPROVED IMMUTABLE PATCH OVERLAY ---\\n\\n--- END NODE PROMPT ---\\n\"\n      ],\n      \"exit_code\": 0,\n      \"finished_at\": \"2026-08-12T18:09:01.647938+00:00\",\n      \"log\": \"/Users/filipepinto/Projects/curriculum_builder/plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/results/v3/logs/N40_CLI_CUTOVER/attempt-20260812T180522.724742Z-82022fe842.claude.log\",\n      \"log_sha256\": \"424242d65df5545463d7ed905f7a1669d0afef8fb8afd2206ca6541fd93ab683\",\n      \"started_at\": \"2026-08-12T18:05:24.679849+00:00\",\n      \"tail\": \"absent, legacy flags (`--lab-id`, etc.) are rejected with exit 2, and no Plan 25 symbol/module is referenced in `runtime/run_curriculum.py` (via AST scan).\\\\n- Left `RunCurriculumElapsedTimeTests` untouched except fixing the shared import.\\\\n- `runtime/run_curriculum.py` and `tests/runtime/test_plan26_cli.py` unchanged (hashes verified identical to generation 1).\\\\n- Updated `results/N40_CLI_CUTOVER.result.v1.md` w